# Allowlist, not a denylist. This directory is a live ComfyUI Portable install: models alone are
# ~600 GiB, plus python_embeded, venvs, user data and an upstream ComfyUI checkout that has its
# own .git. A denylist that misses one entry tries to commit a 42 GiB safetensors, so everything
# is ignored by default and tracked paths are re-included one by one below.
/*

!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/tools/
!/custom_nodes/
!/*.md
!/inspect_quant.py
!/_check_accel.py
# Launchers (.bat) ficam fora: sao configuracao desta maquina, nao codigo de quantizacao. Desde
# 2026-10-01 o iniciar_comfy.bat (3 modos, descrito em .agent-reference/comfy/09-comandos-launchers.md)
# vive so no disco, como os antigos em _launchers_antigos/.

# Written by /setup-matt-pocock-skills: where issues live, the triage vocabulary, and the domain-doc
# rules. Text only, and the skills read them as input on every run -- so untracked here means every
# fresh clone silently loses the conventions and reaches for `gh issue create` against a repo that
# has no remote.
!/docs/

# The per-layer measurements themselves, and only those. A `.analysis.json` is ~60 KiB and is the
# expensive part of this project to reproduce -- it costs a calibration run on a GPU that is
# shared with another session. The `.calib.pt` files beside them are the raw activation samples,
# 170-384 MiB each and 2.2 GiB in total, and they are an input to the analysis rather than a
# result: kept out.
!/calib/
/calib/*
!/calib/*.analysis.json

# Generated by tools/quant_audit.py from whatever is on disk, so it describes this machine rather
# than the code. Regenerable in one command.
/quantization_inventory.json
/quantization_inventory.md

# Nothing but source in the tracked trees. Written generically on purpose: the first version
# of this named tools/ only, and __pycache__ from custom_nodes/ went straight into a commit.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
tools/calib/
tools/bench/

# Saida de `torch.utils.cpp_extension.load`: .pyd, .o, .lib e o cache do ninja. Regeneravel em
# ~60 s por `tools/sparse24_sm86/roda.bat`, e o .pyd sozinho passa de 1 MB. Entrou no stage na
# primeira tentativa de commit porque o allowlist deste arquivo re-inclui `tools/` inteiro.
# `build*` e nao `build`: o primeiro padrao era `tools/*/build/` e nao pegou
# `build_int/`, que entrou no stage na tentativa seguinte.
tools/*/build*/

# bench/ guarda os CRITERIOS escritos antes de medir -- os arquivos em que toda a metodologia
# deste repo se apoia -- no meio de 282 MB de PNG e de latentes `.pt` que sao saida regeneravel.
# Ate 2026-09-01 nao havia re-inclusao nenhuma aqui, entao todo criterio que esta rastreado
# chegou por `git add -f` e todo criterio NOVO ficava de fora em silencio:
#
#     git check-ignore -v bench/criterio_camada2_despacho.md
#     .gitignore:5:/*    bench/criterio_camada2_despacho.md
#
# Achado ao commitar a camada 2 e ver o proprio criterio dela nao entrar. Junto veio o
# `bench/criterio_hunyuan_misto.md`, que estava solto no disco a dias -- a UM `git clean -xdf`
# de sumir. E exatamente a armadilha que este arquivo ja documenta logo abaixo para o
# `.scratch/`, e esta durava mais tempo.
#
# O criterio de o que entra: markdown (criterios, cards do HuggingFace, licencas) entra;
# imagem, latente e log ficam de fora. Um `.json` de resultado que alguem queira rastrear
# continua sendo `git add -f` deliberado, como o `bench/guarda_referencia.json`.
# Mudancas nossas dentro do checkout do ComfyUI, que o repo raiz NAO rastreia. Sem isto elas
# existem so como diff sujo la dentro, e update/update_comfyui.bat as apaga sem avisar. O patch
# fica aqui versionado; o arquivo vivo continua sendo o de ComfyUI/.
!/patches/
/patches/*
!/patches/*.patch
!/patches/README.md
!/patches/tests/
!/patches/arquivo/

!/bench/
/bench/*
!/bench/*.md
!/bench/hf/
/bench/hf/*
!/bench/hf/*/
/bench/hf/*/*
!/bench/hf/*/*.md
!/bench/hf/*/*.txt

# The local issue tracker. Ignored for four days, which meant 26 tickets and the map
# existed only on disk -- one `git clean -xdf` from gone. Tracked now.
!/.scratch/

# But `!/.scratch/` re-includes the WHOLE subtree, and by 2026-08-29 that subtree held 59 GiB of
# payload that `git add -A` would have taken: a 20 GiB model copy, a 37 GiB HF cache, and two
# directories of downloaded upstream workflow templates at 2.0 GiB and 412 MiB. The allowlist above
# exists precisely to stop that, and this is the hole it leaked through -- the tickets are text,
# the scratch space beside them is not. Measured with `du -sh` before writing these five lines.
/.scratch/glm46v_model/
/.scratch/hf_cache/
/.scratch/workflow_templates_upstream/
/.scratch/workflow_templates_upstream_incomplete_20260826/

# Written by tools/gpu_lock.ps1 while the heartbeat runs. Machine state, not source.
tools/.gpu_lock_beat_pid

# O posto de escuta. Texto e ledger, sem payload -- nada de peso baixado entra aqui.
!/research/

# Token de ESCRITA do HuggingFace mora em .hf/token (W4A4_HANDOFF.md:611).
# Nada vazou -- conferido nos 260 commits por quatro caminhos -- mas nada impedia.
.hf/

# Model/checkpoint payloads created by experiments must stay out of Git.
/.scratch/**/*.safetensors
/.scratch/**/*.pt
/.scratch/**/*.pth
/.scratch/**/*.ckpt

# Agent references are source documentation; keep binary payloads excluded.
!/.agent-reference/
/.agent-reference/**
!/.agent-reference/**/
!/.agent-reference/**/*.md

# .scratch guarda texto (tickets, criterios, scripts, resultados .md/.json pequenos). Imagem, video,
# audio, pacote e log sao saida regeneravel ou grande: em 2026-10-01 um `git add -A` levaria 560 MB,
# quase tudo PNG de folhas de contato e renders. Um arquivo desses que precise entrar vai com `git add -f`.
/.scratch/**/*.png
/.scratch/**/*.jpg
/.scratch/**/*.jpeg
/.scratch/**/*.webp
/.scratch/**/*.gif
/.scratch/**/*.mp4
/.scratch/**/*.webm
/.scratch/**/*.wav
/.scratch/**/*.flac
/.scratch/**/*.mp3
/.scratch/**/*.zip
/.scratch/**/*.whl
/.scratch/**/*.log
/.scratch/**/*.err
/.scratch/**/*.pid
/.scratch/object_info_*.json
/.scratch/**/*.bat
/.scratch/pip_2026-09-29/dryrun.json
/.scratch/revisao_2026-09-29/conv/prova/selecao_real_*.json
